    "title": "What time is Sebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman? Fight date, ring walks",
    "text": "Updated March 27, 2026, 11:12 a.m. CTFormer world champion Keith Thurman will challenge Sebastian Fundora for the WBC junior middleweight title in Las Vegas.The pay-per-view event will be broadcast on Prime Video and costs $74.99.A former world boxing champion looks to add another piece of hardware to his collection on March 28, as Keith Thurman challenges the reigning WBC junior middleweight champion Sebastian Fundora in Las Vegas.Despite just two bouts in the past six years, Thurman is back fighting for a world title after an impressive return to the ring last March, stopping Brock Jarvis in the third round on Jarvis's home turf in Australia. He was then slated to face Fundora in October, before Fundora suffered a hand injury which postponed the bout.Fundora, considered by many to be the division's top fighter, is the tallest world champion in boxing towering at 6-foot-5½. He's in the midst of a career-best run in which he became unified champion before twice defending his WBC title, most recently stopping Tim Tszyu in the seventh round of their rematch last July.“I have to expect the best Keith Thurman to come out,\" Fundora said on March 11. \"That’s what we’re training for. Whether he brings it or not, that’s not up to me. But I’ll be ready.\"Here's when the fighters are expected to enter the ring on fight night.Watch Sebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman on Prime Video PPVSebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman date, timeThe PBC on Prime Video pay-per-view card is set to begin at 7 p.m. (CT) on March 28, with ring walks for the main event expected at approximately 10 p.m. (CT). Three preliminary fights will air free on Prime Video beginning at 4:30 p.m. (CT).PPV start: 7 p.m. CTFundora vs. Thurman ring walks: approx. 10 p.m. CTWhere to watch Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman?The Sebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman headlined fight card will air live on Prime Video pay-per-view, while three preliminary fights will stream free on Prime Video ahead of the main card. The pay-per-view is also available through traditional cable and satellite outlets.How to watch: Prime Video PPVSebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman pay-per-view pricePBC's four-fight card from Las Vegas is available on Prime Video pay-per-view, as well as through traditional cable and satellite outlets, for $74.99.PPV price: $74.99Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman fight cardSebastian Fundora (23-1-1, 15 KOs) vs. Keith Thurman (31-1, 23 KOs); WBC junior middleweight titleYoenis Tellez (11-1, 8 KOs) vs. Brian Mendoza (23-4, 17 KOs)Yoenli Hernandez (9-0, 8 KOs) vs. Terrell Gausha (24-5-1, 12 KOs)Gurgen Hovhannisyan (9-0, 8 KOs) vs. Cesar Navarro (15-3, 13 KOs)Preliminary fights (free on Prime Video)Elijah Garcia (17-1, 13 KOs) vs. Kevin Newman II (18-3-1, 11 KOs)Kaipo Gallegos (11-0-1, 9 KOs) vs. Julian Gonzalez (16-1-1, 12 KOs)Brayan Gonzalez (4-0, 3 KOs) vs. Brandon Guerrero (7-4)Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman oddsFundora enters his third title defense as a -380 favorite, while Thurman is a +280 underdog to win the title. The over/under is set at 9.5 rounds.Fundora by KO/TKO: -125Fundora by decision: +255Thurman by KO/TKO: +650Thurman by decision: +600Odds via DraftKings, as of March 26Boxing this weekendMoses Itauma vs. Jermaine Franklin; 1 p.m. (CT), March 28; DAZNSebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman; 7 p.m. (CT), March 28, Prime Video PPVHarrison Campbell covers boxing for The Tennessean and high school sports for The Daily Herald. Email him at hcampbell@usatodayco.com and follow him on Twitter @hccamp.",
